## Tipos de valores básicos ##

<div class="col50p terminal example" style="margin-bottom: -50px;">
document.writeln("&lt;pre>");
document.writeln(123);
document.writeln("Olá");
document.writeln(true);
document.writeln("&lt;/pre>");
</div>
<div class=col50p>
<script>
document.writeln("<pre>");
document.writeln(123);
document.writeln("Olá");
document.writeln(true);
document.writeln("</pre>");
</script>
</div>
<div class=endCols>&nbsp;</div>


* O JavaScript tem 3 tipos primitivos básicos
    * <code class=focus>Number</code> - <span class=litle>(ex: `123`)</span>
    * <code class=focus>String</code> - <span class=litle>(ex: `"Olá"`)</span>
    * <code class=focus>Boolean</code> - <span class=litle>(ex: `true`)</span>
